			"text":"# PPJ AI, Automation & Digital Portfolio — Weekly Status\n\n**As of:** 16 October 2026  \n**Source freshness:** Confirmed discussions through 16 October; latest project artifacts dated 15–16 October. Comparison baseline: 9 October 2026. Older plans are treated as historical baselines.\n\n## 1. Portfolio executive summary\n\n- **Strongest movement:** Sew Agent V1 stabilization is documented, V2 BA support transferred to Nguyễn Vũ Á Khoa, and V2 evidence requirements were defined. Finance WS3 moved into fieldwork with three completed role-based surveys due **22 October**.\n- **Finance constraint clarified:** Separate Weaving and Dyeing OCs do not provide confirmed cross-OC lineage. Finance supplies an OVH report, not confirmed OC-wise OVH. This constrains end-to-end profitability and performance reporting.\n- **Business Travel/WFX progressed:** Accounting supplied detailed 642x and 627x mappings for all 22 expense types. However, all 641x details and 18 of 22 WFX Analysis Code mappings remain open. Production import is not ready.\n- **Operational risk:** Expense-invoice automation is being used, but VAT reset, PDF/XML attachment, airport-invoice linking and slow bulk-processing issues remain unresolved.\n- **No new delivery evidence:** Finance WS1/WS2, GDI/Material Allocation, AWB OCR, GTAS/Stratova, Sourcing/DWH, production forecasting/denim vision, Wizcore and Quansolution.\n\n## 2. Project status\n\n|Project / Workstream|Goal|Tangible Outputs|Current Status|Latest Confirmed Progress|Movement vs 9 Oct|Next Actions|Risks / Blockers|Decision Needed|Owner|Due Date|\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Finance WS1 — Chatbot|Controlled Finance Q&A|Chatbot, access controls, governed answers|Development/validation|**No new confirmed update.**|None confirmed|Confirm access and UAT criteria|Permissions, traceability, Finance validation|Approve source access and UAT owner|Not confirmed|Not confirmed|\n|Finance WS2 — Consolidated Reporting|Automate recurring reporting|Scheduled flow, multi-user app, refresh/history|Partial build|**No new confirmed update.** Prior baseline: session isolation fixed and periodic refresh available; daily operation not confirmed.|None confirmed|Complete access, scheduler, history and user test|Source freshness, scheduler reliability|Confirm production-run owner and go-live gate|Not confirmed|Not confirmed|\n|Finance WS3 — Factory Performance|Define factory cost, labor and production requirements|Three 20-question role-based surveys|Discovery/fieldwork|Surveys created for Accounting/Cost, HR/Payroll and Planning/Production/GTAS.|Planning → response collection|Collect responses and create data/rule/gap register|Response quality and SME availability|Mandate participation; assign consolidation owner|Not confirmed|**22 Oct 2026**|\n|Finance WS4 — Fabric OC|Measure stage/OC cost and performance|OC mapping, tolerance rules, stage-cost logic|Discovery; constrained|Separate Weaving/Dyeing OCs lack confirmed linkage. OVH is report-level, not confirmed OC-wise. The 10% NPL tolerance remains confirmed.|Constraints confirmed|Decide lineage bridge; verify GRN and OVH allocation|1-to-many lineage; OVH allocation; missing field lineage|Approve mapping approach and OVH driver|Finance/Accounting + IT; accountable owner not confirmed|Not confirmed|\n|Finance WS5|Confirm scope|Approved scope and deliverables|Open gap|**No current source confirms an active WS5 scope.**|None|Confirm scope or remove from active portfolio|Portfolio ambiguity|Scope decision|Not confirmed|Not confirmed|\n|Business Travel / HCQT / eOffice / WFX|Integrate approval, settlement and accounting|Category, Analysis Code and GL mapping|Mapping validation|All 22 expense types have 642x/627x details; none has 641x. Four Name3 examples are evidenced.|Material progress|Close 641x, Name3, organizational, VAT and posting rules; run 641/642/627 golden cases|18 Name3 gaps; conflicting 6421 vs 6427/6428 evidence; release readiness|Approve mapping authority, exceptions, effective date and UAT gate|Accounting + HCQT + IT/WFX|Not confirmed|\n|Expense Invoice Automation|Automate invoice intake and evidence attachment|Bulk intake, VAT and PDF/XML handling|Active use; defect-heavy|36 fuel invoices uploaded. VAT resets after Tax Template selection; attachment and airport-invoice linkage issues persist.|At risk|Triage defects and run regression testing|Manual re-entry, incomplete evidence, duplicate/error risk|Assign hotfix and UAT owner|Technical team not named|Not confirmed|\n|GDI / Material Allocation / GRN / Invoice Downloader|Automate WFX material and document flows|APIs and transaction automation|Dependency blocked/support|**No new confirmed update.**|None confirmed|Confirm WFX endpoints, fields and test cases|WFX dependency and master-data quality|Set integration priority and system owner|Not confirmed|Not confirmed|\n|Warehouse / AWB OCR|Extract shipment data|OCR, validation and downstream handoff|Testing baseline|**No new confirmed update.**|None confirmed|Confirm test set, exceptions and integration target|Scan quality and document variation|Confirm UAT scope and operational owner|Not confirmed|Not confirmed|\n|PERRI Costing — Sew/Wash/Technical Knowledge|Automate process and SAM analysis|Sew V1, user guide, fixes, dictionary and V2 evidence pack|V1 stabilization; V2 discovery|Sew V1 completion confirmed. Reported search, ordering, SAM, QC-exclusion, export and operation-existence defects are documented as fixed. V2 BA bridge transferred to **Nguyễn Vũ Á Khoa**.|Major movement|Obtain complete golden case, dictionary and mandatory operations; collect controlled V1 feedback. **Wash Agent: No new confirmed update.**|Incomplete expert data, scope growth, no committed V2 date|Approve V2 boundary, acceptance owner and pilot criteria|Nguyễn Vũ Á Khoa — BA bridge; complete accountability not confirmed|Not confirmed; six months is an estimate, not commitment|\n|KPI/BSC Performance Management|Connect SOP–JD–KPI–Work Done|AS-IS assessment, hierarchy and evidence model|Discovery|Structured BA assessment and management package developed. Direct WFX/Jira/DWH integration is not confirmed.|Concept → structured discovery|Inventory SOP/JD/KPI and evidence sources; define MVP|Repeated setup, unclear evidence ownership|Name sponsor and approve MVP/BRD boundary|Not confirmed|Not confirmed|\n|Smart Factory / Cowash / Hanger / Wizcore|Enable operational production decisions|Process push, performance data and real-time use cases|Discovery; Wizcore deferred|Cowash and Hanger data flows clarified. End-of-day data is insufficient for bottleneck detection; near-real-time events are required.|Requirements advanced; no build restart|Assess latency, machine list and one measurable use case|Facility readiness, latency and vendor dependency|Approve readiness gate and use case|Not confirmed|Not confirmed|\n|Sourcing / PERRI Hub / Dashboards / DWH|Govern assistants and reusable data products|Sourcing assistant, PERRI, datamarts and dashboards|Support/development baseline|**No new confirmed update.**|None confirmed|Reconfirm backlog and data ownership|Fragmented priorities, source quality and access|Confirm portfolio priority and support capacity|Not confirmed|Not confirmed|\n|GTAS / Stratova|Validate production AI opportunities|Pilot scope, data requirements and acceptance criteria|Validation/awaiting decision|**No new confirmed update.**|None confirmed|Confirm data access and acceptance gate|Unconfirmed business acceptance|Continue, reshape or pause|Not confirmed|Not confirmed|\n|Forecasting / Denim Vision & Quotation|Explore forecasting and vision-assisted quotation|Candidate PoC and data requirements|Discovery|**No new confirmed delivery update.**|None confirmed|Select one measurable PoC|Data readiness and sponsorship|Select PoC or retain in discovery|Not confirmed|Not confirmed|\n|PPJ × UIT / AISC|Structure academic collaboration|Judges, topics, presentations, rubric and schedule|Coordination|Preliminary-round judge preparation underway. UIT contract and remaining PPJ documents are pending.|Event preparation active|Obtain pre-read materials and close contract documents|Incomplete preparation and signature delay|Confirm panel and document responsibilities|Not confirmed|**22 Oct 2026**|\n|Quansolution B2C|Deploy when business conditions permit|Production rollout|Strategic hold|**No new confirmed update.**|None|Define restart triggers|Liquidity and commercial timing|Continue hold or approve restart criteria|Not confirmed|Not confirmed|\n\n## 3. Cross-project dependencies and resource conflicts\n\n1. Accounting/WFX specialists are shared across WS4, Business Travel, invoice automation, GDI/GRN and Finance reporting.\n2. WFX master data, APIs and dimensions affect travel posting, material flows, OC profitability and consolidated reporting.\n3. Business experts are simultaneously needed for Finance rules, Sew V2 golden cases, invoice regression and WS3 surveys.\n4. AI/BA capacity is divided across Sew V2, Finance AI, KPI/BSC and production support.\n5. Production-data latency and facility readiness constrain Smart Factory independently of dashboard development.\n\n## 4. Milestone movement\n\n- **Completed:** Three WS3 surveys created; Sew Agent V1 completion confirmed; documented Sew V1 defect set reported fixed.\n- **Moved forward:** HCQT 642x/627x mapping, Sew V2 handover, KPI/BSC assessment, Smart Factory data requirements and Fabric OC constraint discovery.\n- **Delayed or at risk:** Business Travel production mapping, invoice automation stability, Fabric OC end-to-end attribution and WFX-dependent GDI/Material Allocation.\n- **No confirmed movement:** Finance WS1/WS2, AWB, GTAS/Stratova, Sourcing/DWH, forecasting/vision, Wizcore and Quansolution.\n\n## 5. Top five actions for next week\n\n1. Close Fabric OC lineage, GRN source and OVH allocation decisions.\n2. Complete Business Travel 641x/Name3 rules and run WFX posting golden cases.\n3. Prioritize the invoice-automation defect cycle.\n4. Complete the Sew V2 evidence pack and start structured V1 pilot feedback.\n5. Drive WS3 survey completion by 22 October and consolidate requirements.\n\n## 6. Management decisions required\n\n1. **P0:** Approve the Fabric OC cross-OC mapping approach and OVH allocation driver.\n2. **P0:** Confirm the Business Travel accounting authority, exception rules, effective date and UAT gate.\n3. **P0:** Assign invoice-automation defect and UAT ownership.\n4. **P1:** Mandate WS3 participation and appoint the requirements owner.\n5. **P1:** Approve Sew V2 discovery boundaries, golden-case minimum and acceptance owner.\n6. **P1:** Confirm the PPJ × UIT/AISC panel and contract/document responsibilities.\n7. **P2:** Appoint the KPI/BSC sponsor and authorize a bounded MVP/BRD phase.\n8. **P2:** Keep Smart Factory vendor development gated by a measurable use case and readiness review.\n\nKey evidence: HCQT_WFX_AccountingMapping_v2.1.1_MrsViolet_641Update.xlsx, Cập nhật sửa lỗi Sew Agent.pdf, Summary_14102026.txt, Perri Chatbot Costing Book.pdf, and PPJ_GL_COA_TT99_2026_Master_Research.xlsx.",
